# Env files. The glob matters: listing only `.env` and `.env.local` left
# `.env.production` (and any other suffix) committable at the repo root, while
# frontend/meong-my-way/.gitignore already used `.env*`. CI asserts this
# coverage — see .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml.
.env*
!.env.example
.claude
.agents

# Terraform — regenerated by `terraform init`/`apply`, never committed.
# .terraform.lock.hcl is intentionally NOT ignored: it pins provider versions
# and should be committed.
iac/.terraform/
iac/terraform.tfstate
iac/terraform.tfstate.backup
iac/*.tfvars
iac/*.tfvars.json
iac/*.tfplan
iac/crash.log

# Built by `terraform apply` from the handler next to each — the source is
# committed, the zip is not.
lambda/jobs-scraper/jobs-scraper.zip
lambda/courses-scraper/courses-scraper.zip

# Remove all docs and reasoning.
#
# `docs/*` excludes the subdirectories themselves, and git does not descend into
# an excluded directory — so a file added under `docs/` after this rule landed is
# silently untracked, however specific a later negation is. That is not
# theoretical: it is why README.md's architecture diagram 404'd on GitHub while
# rendering perfectly in a local preview, and why ADR-0002 was unreachable from
# the two places the README links it. Files tracked before the rule (ADR-0001,
# the other diagrams) were unaffected, which is what made the gap look arbitrary.
#
# So anything README.md points at has to be re-included explicitly, and the
# directory has to be re-included before the file inside it can be. Add the
# parent-dir pair as well as the file when publishing a new doc asset.
docs/*
!docs/architecture.excalidraw

!docs/adr/
docs/adr/*
!docs/adr/0002-claude-haiku-for-grounded-advice.md

!docs/img/
docs/img/*
!docs/img/architecture-excalidraw.svg

docs/auth
CLAUDE.md
skills-lock.json
strong-software-engineer - Copy.pdf
weak-generalist - Copy.pdf
brag-output*/
